---
import Layout from '../../components/layout/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from '../../config';
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';

const title = 'Cookie Policy - Types, Purpose and How to Manage Them';
const description = 'What cookies we use, their purpose and duration. Step-by-step instructions to manage and disable cookies in your browser to control your privacy settings.';

const schemas = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', url: '/en/' },
    { name: 'Cookie Policy', url: '/en/cookie-policy/' },
  ]),
];
const faqPage = [
  { question: 'What cookies does this site use?', answer: 'Analytics cookies set by Microsoft Clarity (_clck, _clsk) and Google Analytics (_ga), which load when a page opens. No advertising or profiling cookies are set, and the calculators themselves store nothing: every computation runs in your browser and is discarded when the tab closes.' },
  { question: 'Can I refuse analytics cookies?', answer: 'Yes, through your browser settings: block third-party cookies, or the domains clarity.ms and googletagmanager.com. The site shows no consent banner at present. Refusing these cookies does not limit any feature of the site.' },
  { question: 'Do you share data with third parties?', answer: 'Browsing data (pages viewed, clicks, scrolling, device type) is processed by Microsoft Clarity and Google Analytics. No salary figure and no calculation input is transmitted: input fields are masked before anything is sent.' },
  { question: 'How long do the cookies last?', answer: 'The Clarity cookie _clck lasts one year and _clsk one day. The Google Analytics cookies _ga and _ga_6FGRX7NXRF last two years.' },
];
const faqPageSchema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faqPage.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.question, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.answer } })) };
import ContextoFiscal from '../../components/ContextoFiscal.astro';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} schema={schemas} locale="en">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-8">
    <nav class="mb-6 text-sm text-medium-gray">
      <a href="/en/" class="hover:text-brand">Home</a> / <span class="text-charcoal dark:text-gray-200">Cookie Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold text-charcoal md:text-4xl dark:text-gray-100">Cookie Policy</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none text-dark-gray dark:text-gray-300 space-y-6">
      <p><em>Last updated: June {new Date().getFullYear()}</em> This page explains which cookies this site sets, why, and how to refuse them. Technical cookies needed to display pages and remember your language require no consent. Audience measurement cookies tell us which pages are useful and which need rewriting; they are configured so that they cannot follow a visitor from one site to another, and advertising features are disabled. You can delete all of them from your browser settings at any time, and the site works normally in a browser that blocks them. No cookie on this site records the salary figures you enter into a calculator. Audience data is kept for no more than fourteen months, after which the measurement tools delete it themselves, and it is never sold or shared for advertising.</p>

      <p>
        At <strong>{SITE_NAME}</strong> ({SITE_URL}), we value your privacy. This cookie policy explains
        what cookies and storage technologies we use and which we do not, in compliance with the GDPR
        (Regulation EU 2016/679), the Spanish LOPDGDD (Organic Law 3/2018), and Article 22.2 of the LSSI-CE.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files that websites store on your computer or mobile device when you visit
        them. They are widely used to make websites function correctly, improve user experience, and provide
        information to website owners. Cookies can be classified into several categories: strictly necessary
        cookies, functional cookies, analytics cookies, and marketing cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        European legislation, particularly the ePrivacy Directive and the GDPR, requires websites to inform
        users about cookie usage and, in many cases, obtain consent before placing cookies. Strictly
        necessary cookies are exempt from this requirement and may be placed without consent.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">2. Does This Website Use Cookies?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Yes.</strong> This website sets third-party analytics cookies through Microsoft Clarity and
        Google Analytics 4. Both tools load when a page opens, with no prior cookie banner. No advertising
        cookies are placed.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">3. Analytics Tools</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> (Microsoft Corporation) records how pages are used: clicks,
        scrolling, pages viewed and their address, as sessions and heatmaps. The content of input fields is
        masked in your browser before anything is sent. Clarity sets the cookies <code>_clck</code> (one
        year) and <code>_clsk</code> (one day); Microsoft may also set <code>MUID</code> and
        <code>CLID</code> on its own domains. More information:
        <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" class="text-brand hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (Google Ireland Limited) receives the pages viewed, the referral
        source, the device type and an approximate location derived from the IP address. It sets the
        cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_6FGRX7NXRF</code> (two years). More information:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-brand hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Data collected by Microsoft Clarity and Google Analytics may be processed on servers located in
        the United States. Microsoft and Google rely on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and on standard
        contractual clauses. Clarity keeps session recordings for thirty days and aggregated data for no more than thirteen
        months; Google Analytics keeps event data for the period set in the account, fourteen months at
        most.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">4. Functional Storage (localStorage)</h2>
      <p>
        Our website stores your theme preference (light or dark mode) and potential language preferences in
        your browser using <strong>localStorage</strong>. This is not a cookie but a local storage method
        provided by the HTML5 standard. localStorage differs from cookies in important ways:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Data is <strong>not sent to our servers</strong> with page requests</li>
        <li>Data is <strong>not traceable</strong> to you as a person</li>
        <li>You can delete the data through your browser settings</li>
        <li>The storage is strictly necessary for website functionality</li>
        <li>No information is shared with third parties</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Since localStorage is not a cookie and data is never sent to external servers, it falls under the
        exemption for strictly necessary technical storage and no prior consent is required.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">5. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Our website may load web fonts from third-party content delivery networks. When you access a page,
        your browser loads the required fonts from external servers, which may receive your IP address as
        part of the standard HTTP request. This usage is based on our legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR)
        in a uniform and attractive presentation of our website.
      </p>
      <p>
        Apart from Microsoft Clarity and Google Analytics (see section 3), we do not integrate other
        third-party services. There are no social media buttons, advertising widgets or remarketing services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">6. Cookie Banner</h2>
      <p>
        This website currently shows no cookie banner: the analytics cookies listed above are set when a
        page opens. You can refuse them by blocking third-party cookies, or the domains
        <code>clarity.ms</code> and <code>googletagmanager.com</code>, in your browser settings. The
        calculators work without them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">7. How to Manage Cookies in Your Browser</h2>
      <p>
        Most web browsers allow you to manage cookies through their settings. You can reject cookies,
        delete existing ones, or set your browser to alert you when a cookie is placed. Refer to your
        browser's help for specific instructions:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline">Google Chrome</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline">Mozilla Firefox</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline">Safari</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline">Microsoft Edge</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Please note that blocking all cookies may affect the functionality of some websites.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">8. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR and LOPDGDD, you have the right to be informed about the use of cookies and storage
        technologies. For the data collected through the analytics cookies, you can exercise your GDPR rights by
        writing to the contact address. You always have the right to reject cookies, delete localStorage data, lodge
        a complaint with the AEPD, and contact us with questions about our cookie policy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">9. Changes and Contact</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to modify this cookie policy to reflect changes in our practices or applicable
        law. The current version is always available on this page. For questions, contact us at:<br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:contact@elsueldoneto.es" class="text-brand hover:underline">contact@elsueldoneto.es</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-charcoal dark:text-gray-100">10. Related Pages</h2>
      <p>
        See also our <a href="/en/privacy-policy/" class="text-brand hover:underline">privacy policy</a> and
        our <a href="/en/legal-notice/" class="text-brand hover:underline">legal notice</a> for more
        information about how we handle your data and the legal aspects of our website.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqPageSchema)} />
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10">
    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      {faqPage.map((f) => (
        <details class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 dark:border-gray-700">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold">{f.question}</summary>
          <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">{f.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContextoFiscal />
</Layout>
